> Is the model you fit an exploratory or confirmatory factor analysis model?
> If the former this is quite common due to the rotational indeterminacy, and
> you could just multiply each axis by -1 to flip the signs for each
> dimension. If the latter, this would be more unusual given the starting
> values of mirt, but the same principle would apply. All latent variable
> models are effectively sign indeterminate if the identification isn't based
> on some anchoring item, and in IRT models we often use the default 0 mean 1
> variance scaling, so this can crop up. HTH.
