> > in the model without covariates, I assume that it is the residual variance
> > that is fixed to one. If that's the case, is there a way to convert these
> > parameters to the same metric so that we can compare them?
>
> Yes, and indeed for any model that doesn't freely estimate the variance of
> the latent trait you should consider changing the identification to the
> version where the latent variable scale is determined by an item (say, item
> 1) by freeing the latent trait variance parameter and setting the slope of
> the identification item to 1. This is actually the default in most SEM
> software, precisely for this reason.
>
> Because this is a simulation study just be careful about the scaling of the
> item parameters and traits. I often will just generate data given that the
> first item slopes is always fixed at 1, and change the latent variance and
> remaining parameters through the simulations. HTH.
>
