It does (I run your code), but they are not going to be exactly the same. Also, the numbers you chose to simulate data are a little extreme, so there might be a lot going on under the hood when you try to estimate these parameters (for instance, your choice of 0.5 for discrimination is pretty low and may produce noisy data, and you have some extremely difficult and easy items based on b parameters). When I run your code, the numbers estimated were reasonable enough compared to the true values.

